  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Fallback and live rules",
      "items": [
        "translateToGloss falls back to the offline engine when the browser is offline, after a 3 s timeout, on a network or non-2xx response, or when no tokens survive; the engine badge then reads \"AI unavailable\" (lib/islTranslator.ts:64-104, page.tsx:424)",
        "Without GEMINI_API_KEY the route returns 500 and never calls Gemini, so a setup without the key falls back on every AI run (route.ts:38-44, .env.example:5)",
        "Live chunks always use the offline engine, queued in spoken order; quick-phrase chips call translateOffline directly and never pass through dispatchTranslation (page.tsx:110-123, 251-256)",
        "Only a new typed run or switching to Offline aborts an in-flight AI call; chips, Live chunks and Stop do not, so a late AI result can still play (page.tsx:125-126, 142-146, 162-165, 279-285)",
        "Voice only fills the input. Live signs interim words as they appear, so later recognizer corrections are not re-signed, and restarts recognition 220 ms after it ends with the word cursor reset (page.tsx:204-236)",
        "Recognition comes from the browser vendor (Chrome sends the audio to Google speech servers); without the API, Voice and Live are disabled (page.tsx:198-201, 431-446)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Vocabulary sanitizing",
      "items": [
        "SUPPORTED_TOKENS (164 signs, lib/islVocabulary.ts:13-29) feeds the Gemini prompt, both translators and AvatarPlayer",
        "sanitizeTokens keeps supported signs and single letters and splits any other token into A–Z letters (islVocabulary.ts:48-63)",
        "Online tokens are sanitized twice: in the route (route.ts:86) and in the browser (islTranslator.ts:89)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "ISL grammar rules",
      "items": [
        "textToGloss tries a phrase dictionary, then a whole-sentence sign match, then drops stopwords, lemmatizes and reorders (textToGloss.js:464-585)",
        "Order: TIME, SUBJECT, OBJECT, other/adjective, VERB, NEGATION, QUESTION (textToGloss.js:562-572)",
        "Pronouns: I/me/we become I, my/our MY, your YOUR, he/she/they PERSON; his/her/their are dropped; it/this/that pass through and are fingerspelled (textToGloss.js:587-614, islVocabulary.ts:54-60)",
        "Gemini gets the same word-order rules (TIME, SOV, negation, WH last) in SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION, with temperature 0 and a JSON string-array schema; its pronoun rule differs and maps him/her to PERSON (route.ts:11-33, 61-75)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Fingerspelling",
      "items": [
        "Names and words outside the vocabulary become single letters in sanitizeTokens; the Gemini prompt also asks for letters (route.ts:29)",
        "AvatarPlayer plays a words.js sign when one is exported, otherwise one A–Z animation per letter (AvatarPlayer.tsx:432-440)",
        "A phrase that is not already playable gloss is re-run through textToGloss inside AvatarPlayer (AvatarPlayer.tsx:415-417)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Avatar timing and easing",
      "items": [
        "Each animation frame moves a bone 0.05 × speed rad toward its target, then holds 170 / speed ms per keyframe (AvatarPlayer.tsx:209-225)",
        "Speed slider 0.5–3 (page.tsx:434, 448); Stop clears the queue, Reset snaps to defaultPose, Live mode appends instead of resetting (AvatarPlayer.tsx:60-84, 400-408)",
        "Default and Human both load ybot.glb; Human adds vertex colours and a procedural face (AvatarPlayer.tsx:138-162)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Deployment: Docker and Vercel",
      "items": [
        "Dockerfile: node:20-alpine builder runs npm install and next build; the runner runs next start on port 3000",
        ".dockerignore excludes .env*, so GEMINI_API_KEY must be supplied when the container runs",
        "RootLayout renders the client <Analytics/> component only when NODE_ENV is production; the browser then loads /_vercel/insights/script.js and sends the beacons (layout.tsx:23)",
        "The Docker runner also sets NODE_ENV=production, but nothing in the app serves /_vercel, so analytics stays inert there; the repo has no vercel.json (Dockerfile:12)",
        "public/models/brunette.glb is still shipped in public/ but no code loads it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Local-only account",
      "items": [
        "Sign in and sign up write {name, email} to localStorage key yap-render-account (page.tsx:296-313)",
        "The password field is required but never stored or checked; no server call is made"
      ]
    }
  ]
